# Next.js data

Specs: `docs/02-architecture.md`, `docs/03-contracts.md` §5–6 and §9, `docs/07-pages-spec.md`.

This Next.js may differ from training data. If an App Router API is unfamiliar, read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using it.

- Page → feature hook → `DataSource` (`NEXT_PUBLIC_DATA_SOURCE=mock|api`) → `/api/*`.
- Components do not call `fetch` or the DataSource. No server actions. No fetching in server components.
- DTOs and error codes come from `src/contracts`. Query keys come from one `qk` factory.
- `useRun` refetches every 2s only when `run.poll` is true.
- Pay, requote, exclude, and discard replace the cache with the returned `RunDetail`. Do not optimistically mark a run paid.
- Server state stays in the query cache. Do not copy it into Zustand or context.
- `page.tsx` renders a client screen. Never import `src/server/**` into client code.
- `/dev/*` and `/api/demo/*` return 404 unless `DEMO_MODE` is true.
- Route handlers: `export const runtime = 'nodejs'` when touching Mongo or Airwallex. Validate, call a service, return the DTO or `{ error: { code, message, fieldErrors? } }`.
- The mock DataSource enforces `allowedActions` and returns `409 INVALID_STATE` otherwise.

```ts
useRun(id, { refetchInterval: (q) => (q.state.data?.poll ? 2000 : false) });
```
